    "print(PROJECT)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3cc73ac6",
   "metadata": {},
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b0351109",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Cargar los datos\n",
    "\n",
    "Usamos la **Opción B** de la guía: leer el CSV desde una URL pública (el archivo *raw* de nuestro repositorio en GitHub). Así el notebook funciona en cualquier Colab sin subir archivos manualmente."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "34071665",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "url = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/danielaestudio02-del/Despliegue_cafe_ml2/main/clean_cafe_saless.csv\"\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(url)\n",
    "df.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d2bd6aca",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Revisión mínima del dataset"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "e0a0a81c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(df.shape)\n",
    "display(df.head())\n",
    "display(df.dtypes)\n",
    "display(df.isna().sum().sort_values(ascending=False).head(15))\n",
    "display(df.describe(include=\"all\").T)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f3e384c0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Respuestas a las preguntas de la guía\n",
    "\n",
    "- **¿Qué representa una fila?** Una **transacción** de venta en la cafetería (no un cliente).\n",
    "- **¿Cuál es el objetivo del análisis?** Descubrir **tipos de compra** sin una respuesta conocida (aprendizaje no supervisado, Ruta B).\n",
    "- **¿Qué variables pueden entrar al modelo?**\n",
    "  - Numéricas: `Quantity`, `Price Per Unit`, `Total Spent`.\n",
    "  - `Transaction ID` es un identificador → **no** se usa (la guía pide no incluir identificadores).\n",
    "  - `Transaction Date` es una fecha → **no** se usa; no tiene sentido como entrada para un caso nuevo en la app.\n",
    "  - `Item`, `Payment Method`, `Location` son categóricas → la guía recomienda empezar con numéricas interpretables, así que en esta versión base no se usan.\n",
    "- **¿Hay datos faltantes?** No; el dataset ya viene limpio.\n",
    "- **¿Hay variables numéricas y categóricas?** Sí, ambas (ver tabla de `dtypes`)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3d171621",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Observaciones adicionales sobre los datos"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "29e62a43",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Total Spent debería ser Quantity x Price Per Unit. ¿Se cumple siempre?\n",
    "coincide = df[\"Total Spent\"] == df[\"Quantity\"] * df[\"Price Per Unit\"]\n",
    "print(f\"Filas donde Total Spent == Quantity * Price Per Unit: {coincide.sum()} ({coincide.mean():.1%})\")\n",
    "print(f\"Filas donde NO coincide: {(~coincide).sum()} ({(~coincide).mean():.1%})\")\n",
    "display(df.loc[~coincide, [\"Item\", \"Quantity\", \"Price Per Unit\", \"Total Spent\"]].head(10))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Precio por producto\n",
    "display(pd.crosstab(df[\"Item\"], df[\"Price Per Unit\"]))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Valores posibles de las variables numéricas\n",
    "for col in [\"Quantity\", \"Price Per Unit\", \"Total Spent\"]:\n",
    "    print(col, sorted(df[col].unique()))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7d718f4f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Limitaciones que reconocemos:**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **`Total Spent` es casi redundante:** en teoría es `Quantity × Price Per Unit`, y así se cumple en ~89% de las filas. La mantenemos para seguir la guía (usar las numéricas disponibles), pero hace que el gasto total pese más al formar los grupos.\n",
    "2. **Datos muy discretos:** `Quantity` va de 1 a 5 y `Price Per Unit` toma pocos valores, por lo que hay pocas combinaciones distintas. Los clusters dividen esa \"cuadrícula\" más que descubrir grupos naturales.\n",
    "3. **Posible imputación previa:** cada producto tiene un precio fijo, pero algunas filas tienen precio 3.0 en productos que no cuestan eso (ver tabla). Además, en ~11% de las filas `Total Spent` no coincide con cantidad × precio, y los valores que se repiten (cantidad 3, precio 3.0, total 8.0) son justo las medianas. Probablemente quien limpió la base rellenó faltantes con la mediana. En esta versión base no corregimos estas filas; se deja documentado.\n",
    "4. **Unidad de análisis:** como cada fila es una transacción, los clusters se interpretan como **tipos de compra**, no como perfiles de cliente."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "aa3b2aa0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Definir variables (Paso 9.1 de la guía)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "dcd5b9a2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "numeric_features = [\n",
    "    \"Quantity\",\n",
    "    \"Price Per Unit\",\n",
    "    \"Total Spent\"\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "features = numeric_features\n",
    "X = df[features].copy()\n",
    "X.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7239a392",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Preprocesamiento + K-Means (Paso 9.2 de la guía)\n",
    "\n",
    "Todo va dentro de un `Pipeline`, así las mismas transformaciones del entrenamiento se aplican automáticamente cuando Streamlit reciba un nuevo caso. `random_state=42` garantiza que los clusters sean los mismos cada vez que se entrena (reproducibilidad)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0ec57d9b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n",
    "from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "from sklearn.cluster import KMeans\n",
    "\n",
    "model = Pipeline([\n",
    "    (\"imputer\", SimpleImputer(strategy=\"median\")),\n",
    "    (\"scaler\", StandardScaler()),\n",
    "    (\"cluster\", KMeans(\n",
    "        n_clusters=3,\n",
    "        random_state=42,\n",
    "        n_init=\"auto\"\n",
    "    ))\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "labels = model.fit_predict(X)\n",
    "pd.Series(labels).value_counts().sort_index()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b5cdad81",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Evaluar estructura (Paso 9.3 de la guía)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b8f57e4d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.metrics import silhouette_score\n",
    "\n",
    "X_processed = model[:-1].transform(X)\n",
    "\n",
    "score = silhouette_score(X_processed, labels)\n",
    "print(\"Silhouette:\", round(score, 3))\n",
    "print(\"Inercia:\", round(model[-1].inertia_, 2))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0e548bd9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "El Silhouette va de -1 a 1; valores cercanos a 0.4 indican una estructura **aceptable** (grupos razonablemente separados, aunque no perfectamente). Como dice la guía, no existe una métrica única que \"demuestre\" que los clusters son correctos: combinamos esta evidencia con la interpretabilidad de los perfiles."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f47e0305",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Interpretar los clusters (Sección 10 de la guía)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c0dd6228",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df_clustered = df.copy()\n",
    "df_clustered[\"cluster\"] = labels\n",
    "\n",
    "profiles = (\n",
    "    df_clustered\n",
    "    .groupby(\"cluster\")[numeric_features]\n",
    "    .mean()\n",
    "    .round(2)\n",
    ")\n",
    "profiles[\"n_transacciones\"] = df_clustered[\"cluster\"].value_counts().sort_index()\n",
    "\n",
    "display(profiles)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "22046831",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Productos más frecuentes en cada cluster (ayuda a nombrar los perfiles)\n",
    "display(pd.crosstab(df_clustered[\"cluster\"], df_clustered[\"Item\"]))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a78e8962",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "A partir de la tabla de perfiles nombramos los clusters. Los nombres **surgen de los datos**: se generan automáticamente comparando cada promedio con el promedio general (alto/bajo), para que no dependan de qué número le asignó K-Means a cada grupo."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "38f44d45",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "overall = df[numeric_features].mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "def nivel(valor, media, femenino=False):\n",
    "    if valor >= media:\n",
    "        return \"alta\" if femenino else \"alto\"\n",
    "    return \"baja\" if femenino else \"bajo\"\n",
    "\n",
    "cluster_descriptions = {}\n",
    "for c, row in profiles.iterrows():\n",
    "    cluster_descriptions[int(c)] = (\n",
    "        f\"Cantidad {nivel(row['Quantity'], overall['Quantity'], femenino=True)} \"\n",
    "        f\"(~{row['Quantity']:.1f} uds), \"\n",
    "        f\"precio unitario {nivel(row['Price Per Unit'], overall['Price Per Unit'])} \"\n",
    "        f\"(~${row['Price Per Unit']:.2f}), \"\n",
    "        f\"gasto total {nivel(row['Total Spent'], overall['Total Spent'])} \"\n",
    "        f\"(~${row['Total Spent']:.2f})\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "cluster_descriptions"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c030c9d4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Guardar el artefacto `model.joblib`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3317c589",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import joblib\n",
    "\n",
    "artifact = {\n",
    "    \"model\": model,\n",
    "    \"features\": features,\n",
    "    \"numeric_features\": numeric_features,\n",
    "    \"task\": \"clustering\",\n",
    "    \"cluster_descriptions\": cluster_descriptions\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "joblib.dump(\n",
    "    artifact,\n",
    "    PROJECT / \"model.joblib\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(\"Guardado en\", PROJECT / \"model.joblib\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "484fac7c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "El artefacto contiene el modelo y la información que la app de Streamlit necesita para construir la interfaz. **Este es el \"contrato\" con la parte de despliegue:** las llaves `model`, `features`, `numeric_features`, `task` y `cluster_descriptions`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6c92d4ca",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Convertir el entrenamiento en `train.py` (Secciones 11 y 12 de la guía)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Paso 9.1 — Preparar el dataset dentro del proyecto"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b520fca5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "data_dir = PROJECT / \"data\"\n",
    "data_dir.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "df.to_csv(data_dir / \"clean_cafe_saless.csv\", index=False)\n",
    "print(list(data_dir.iterdir()))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e1290582",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Paso 9.2 — Escribir `train.py`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "9d5f5ea1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%%writefile /content/ml_streamlit_project/train.py\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "import joblib\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from sklearn.cluster import KMeans\n",
    "from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import silhouette_score\n",
    "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "\n",
    "DATA_PATH = Path(\"data/clean_cafe_saless.csv\")\n",
    "MODEL_PATH = Path(\"model.joblib\")\n",
    "\n",
    "NUMERIC_FEATURES = [\"Quantity\", \"Price Per Unit\", \"Total Spent\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def load_data() -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    return pd.read_csv(DATA_PATH)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def describe_clusters(df: pd.DataFrame, labels) -> dict:\n",
    "    df_clustered = df.copy()\n",
    "    df_clustered[\"cluster\"] = labels\n",
    "    profiles = df_clustered.groupby(\"cluster\")[NUMERIC_FEATURES].mean().round(2)\n",
    "    overall = df[NUMERIC_FEATURES].mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "    def nivel(valor, media, femenino=False):\n",
    "        if valor >= media:\n",
    "            return \"alta\" if femenino else \"alto\"\n",
    "        return \"baja\" if femenino else \"bajo\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    descriptions = {}\n",
    "    for c, row in profiles.iterrows():\n",
    "        descriptions[int(c)] = (\n",
    "            f\"Cantidad {nivel(row['Quantity'], overall['Quantity'], femenino=True)} \"\n",
    "            f\"(~{row['Quantity']:.1f} uds), \"\n",
    "            f\"precio unitario {nivel(row['Price Per Unit'], overall['Price Per Unit'])} \"\n",
    "            f\"(~${row['Price Per Unit']:.2f}), \"\n",
    "            f\"gasto total {nivel(row['Total Spent'], overall['Total Spent'])} \"\n",
    "            f\"(~${row['Total Spent']:.2f})\"\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    print(profiles)\n",
    "    return descriptions\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def train_model(df: pd.DataFrame) -> dict:\n",
    "    # 1. Definir variables\n",
    "    features = NUMERIC_FEATURES\n",
    "    X = df[features].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "    # 2. Construir preprocesamiento + modelo\n",
    "    model = Pipeline([\n",
    "        (\"imputer\", SimpleImputer(strategy=\"median\")),\n",
    "        (\"scaler\", StandardScaler()),\n",
    "        (\"cluster\", KMeans(n_clusters=3, random_state=42, n_init=\"auto\")),\n",
    "    ])\n",
    "\n",
    "    # 3. Entrenar\n",
    "    labels = model.fit_predict(X)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # 4. Evaluar\n",
    "    score = silhouette_score(model[:-1].transform(X), labels)\n",
    "    print(f\"Silhouette: {score:.3f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    # 5. Construir artifact\n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"model\": model,\n",
    "        \"features\": features,\n",
    "        \"numeric_features\": NUMERIC_FEATURES,\n",
    "        \"task\": \"clustering\",\n",
    "        \"cluster_descriptions\": describe_clusters(df, labels),\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def main() -> None:\n",
    "    df = load_data()\n",
    "    artifact = train_model(df)\n",
    "    joblib.dump(artifact, MODEL_PATH)\n",
    "    print(f\"Modelo guardado en {MODEL_PATH}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n",
    "    main()"
   ]
  },
  {
