    "## 10. Verificación de reproducibilidad\n",
    "\n",
    "Comprobamos que `train.py` reconstruye **el mismo modelo** que entrenamos en las celdas: cargamos el `model.joblib` generado por el script y verificamos que asigna los mismos clusters a todas las filas."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "4e723f5a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "artifact_loaded = joblib.load(PROJECT / \"model.joblib\")\n",
    "model_loaded = artifact_loaded[\"model\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "labels_script = model_loaded.predict(df[artifact_loaded[\"features\"]])\n",
    "print(\"¿Mismos clusters que en el notebook?\", (labels_script == labels).all())\n",
    "print(\"Llaves del artefacto:\", list(artifact_loaded.keys()))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "84a6700e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Ejemplo de entrada y salida (para el README)\n",
    "\n",
    "La app de Streamlit recibirá un caso nuevo con las mismas columnas. Probamos tres casos distintos:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d9c0c6c2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "casos = pd.DataFrame([\n",
    "    {\"Quantity\": 1, \"Price Per Unit\": 2.0, \"Total Spent\": 2.0},   # 1 café\n",
    "    {\"Quantity\": 5, \"Price Per Unit\": 1.0, \"Total Spent\": 5.0},   # 5 galletas\n",
    "    {\"Quantity\": 4, \"Price Per Unit\": 5.0, \"Total Spent\": 20.0},  # 4 ensaladas\n",
    "], columns=artifact_loaded[\"features\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "casos[\"cluster\"] = model_loaded.predict(casos)\n",
    "casos[\"descripcion\"] = casos[\"cluster\"].map(artifact_loaded[\"cluster_descriptions\"])\n",
    "casos"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "970e5e7e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Versiones de librerías (para `requirements.txt`)\n",
    "\n",
    "Un `model.joblib` guardado con una versión de scikit-learn puede fallar al cargarse con otra versión dentro de Docker. Por eso registramos las versiones exactas usadas para entrenar; la parte de despliegue debe copiarlas en `requirements.txt`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "bf9139e1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sklearn, numpy, joblib as jl, streamlit\n",
    "\n",
    "requirements = f\"\"\"streamlit=={streamlit.__version__}\n",
    "pandas=={pd.__version__}\n",
    "numpy=={numpy.__version__}\n",
    "scikit-learn=={sklearn.__version__}\n",
    "joblib=={jl.__version__}\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "print(requirements)"
   ]
  },
